." $NetBSD$
.Dd February 13, 2026
.Dt JAILMGR 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jailmgr
.Nd provision and manage multiple jailctl jails from one configuration
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility is a shell-script helper around
.Xr jailctl 8
for provisioning and operating multiple jails.
It is designed for setups that use:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
a shared, read-only base filesystem extracted from
.Pa base.tar.xz ,
.It
a per-jail writable
.Pa /.data
mount for mutable state (with base-layer symlinks from
.Pa /etc ,
.Pa /var ,
.Pa /tmp ,
.Pa /home ,
.Pa /root ,
and
.Pa /usr/pkg
into
.Pa /.data ) ,
a jail-local
.Pa /dev ,
and
.It
jail naming and lifecycle management via
.Xr jailctl 8 .
.El
.Pp
By default,
.Nm
reads configuration from
.Pa /etc/jailmgr.conf .
A different configuration file can be selected with the
.Ev JAILMGR_CONF
environment variable.
.Pp
Most commands require superuser privileges.
.Sh COMMANDS
The following commands are supported:
.Bl -tag -width "restart --all"
.It Cm bootstrap
Download
.Pa base.tar.xz
and
.Pa etc.tar.xz
from
.Ev NETBSD_MIRROR
after ensuring the
.Li secmodel_jail
kernel module is loaded,
and persist
.Li secmodel_jail
in
.Pa /etc/modules.conf
for future boots.
Also ensure
.Li jailmgr=
exists in
.Pa /etc/rc.conf
and initialize it to
.Dq NO
if absent.
If
.Pa /etc/jailmgr.conf
does not exist, create it using the running system release normalized to
.Dq major.minor
.Pq e.g. Dq 10.1
so mirror URLs do not include suffixes like
.Dq _STABLE
or
.Dq _RC1 .
Then
extract
.Pa base.tar.xz
into the configured shared base layer directory.
.It Cm create Op Fl a Op Fl s Ar cmd Op Fl c Ar cpu-percent Op Fl m Ar memory-mb Op Fl p Ar profile Op Fl r Ar port[,port...] Op Fl f Ar facility Op Fl o Ar stdout-level Op Fl e Ar stderr-level Op Fl t Ar tag Ar name
Create directories and metadata for one jail:
.Pa root ,
.Pa data ,
and
.Pa dev .
If necessary,
.Pa etc.tar.xz
is extracted into
.Pa data/etc
for that jail.
If host
.Pa /etc/resolv.conf
exists,
it is copied to
.Pa data/etc/resolv.conf
at create time.
A jail-local shell configuration file is written to
.Pa ${JAIL_DATA_DIR}/name/jail.conf .
When
.Fl a
is provided,
.Ev JAIL_AUTOSTART
is initialized to
.Dq YES
in that generated
.Pa jail.conf .
When
.Fl s
is provided,
.Ev JAIL_SUPERVISE_CMD
is initialized to the specified command string in the generated
.Pa jail.conf .
When
.Fl c
.Pq cpu percent from 0 to 100
is provided,
the generated
.Pa jail.conf
stores the corresponding create-time CPU limit used by
.Xr jailctl 8
.Pq internally converted to milliseconds per second; 1% = 10ms/s .
When
.Fl m
.Pq megabytes
is provided,
the generated
.Pa jail.conf
stores the corresponding create-time
.Xr jailctl 8
resource limits
.Pq internally converted to bytes .
When
.Fl p
is provided,
the generated
.Pa jail.conf
stores the corresponding
.Xr jailctl 8
create profile
.Pq Dq low ,
.Dq medium ,
or
.Dq high .
When
.Fl r
is provided,
the generated
.Pa jail.conf
stores the corresponding
.Xr jailctl 8
create-time reserved listening ports
.Pq comma-separated list forwarded to Cm create Fl r .
When
.Fl f ,
.Fl o ,
.Fl e ,
or
.Fl t
is provided,
the generated
.Pa jail.conf
stores the corresponding
.Xr jailctl 8
supervisor logging settings.
.It Cm start Ar name
Mount the composed jail root and start the jail with
.Xr jailctl 8 , using required per-jail settings from
.Pa jail.conf .
.It Cm start Cm --all
Start all jails found under
.Ev JAIL_DATA_DIR
with a
.Pa jail.conf
and
.Ev JAIL_AUTOSTART=YES .
If one jail fails to start, processing continues with the next jail.
.It Cm stop Ar name
Terminate the corresponding
.Xr jailctl 8
supervise process for the jail named
.Ar name ,
then destroy the jail by name through
.Xr jailctl 8
and unmount its root composition.
.It Cm stop Cm --all
Stop and unmount all jails found under
.Ev JAIL_DATA_DIR
with a
.Pa jail.conf
and
.Ev JAIL_AUTOSTART=YES .
.It Cm restart Ar name
Run
.Cm stop
for jail
.Ar name
and then
.Cm start
for the same jail, using the optional settings from
.Pa jail.conf .
.It Cm restart Cm --all
Run
.Cm stop Cm --all
followed by
.Cm start Cm --all .
.It Cm apply Op Cm --ephemeral Ar name Op Ar script | Cm - Op Cm -- Ar arg ...
Execute a shell script inside jail
.Ar name
using
.Xr jexec 8
and
.Pa /bin/sh .
If the jail is not running, it is started first.
The script can be provided as a filesystem path, as
.Cm -
to read from standard input, or omitted when standard input is not a terminal
.Pq for heredoc use .
The script is copied into jail
.Pa /tmp
with a unique temporary filename before execution and removed afterwards.
Arguments after
.Cm --
are passed through to the script.
By default, a jail started for
.Cm apply
remains running.
When
.Cm --ephemeral
is specified, a jail that was started by
.Cm apply
is stopped again after script execution.
.It Cm config Ar name
Open
.Pa ${JAIL_DATA_DIR}/name/jail.conf
for editing in the standard editor for the current environment.
.Nm
uses
.Ev VISUAL
when set,
otherwise
.Ev EDITOR ,
and falls back to
.Cm vi .
.It Cm list
List all configured jails as a table with columns
.Li NAME ,
.Li ROOT ,
.Li SUPERVISE_CMD ,
and
.Li AUTOSTART .
.It Cm status
Show
.Xr jailctl 8
status and mount status for all configured jails.
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
accepts shell-style variable assignments in
.Pa /etc/jailmgr.conf
(or the file referenced by
.Ev JAILMGR_CONF ) .
.Pp
Important variables:
.Bl -tag -width "JAIL_RELEASE_DIR"
.It Ev RELEASE
NetBSD release used for set download paths, in
.Dq major.minor
form only
.Pq no suffixes such as Dq _STABLE , Dq _BETA , Dq _RC1 .
.It Ev MACHINE_ARCH
Machine architecture used for set download paths.
.It Ev NETBSD_MIRROR
Base URL for set downloads.
.It Ev JAIL_BASE_DIR
Directory containing extracted shared base layers.
.It Ev JAIL_DATA_DIR
Directory containing per-jail writable state.
.It Ev JAIL_RELEASE_DIR
Directory containing downloaded set archives.
.It Ev JAIL_LOCAL_DEV
When set to
.Dq YES
(default), mount a jail-local tmpfs on
.Pa /dev
and populate a minimal device set with
.Xr MAKEDEV 8 .
.It Ev JAIL_DEV_SIZE
Size argument used for the tmpfs mounted at jail-local
.Pa /dev
(default
.Dq 8m ) .
.It Ev JAIL_DEVICES
Whitespace-separated list of
.Xr MAKEDEV 8
targets used to populate jail-local
.Pa /dev .
.It Ev JAIL_PTYFS
When set to
.Dq YES
(default), mount
.Xr ptyfs 5
at
.Pa /dev/pts
inside each jail-local
.Pa /dev
to support pseudo terminals.
.El
.Pp
Each jail also has a jail-local configuration file at
.Pa ${JAIL_DATA_DIR}/name/jail.conf
that provides:
.Bl -tag -width "JAIL_SUPERVISE_CMD"
.It Ev JAIL_SUPERVISE_CMD
Required command (with optional arguments) passed to
.Xr jailctl 8
.Cm supervise
after jail creation.
Only the supervised command's stdout/stderr are forwarded to host syslog.
Programs that default to internal syslog logging (for example
.Xr bozohttpd 8
without
.Fl s )
must be configured to emit to stderr if those logs should be captured by
.Nm .
.It Ev JAIL_CREATE_CPU_MS
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr jailctl 8
.Cm create Fl c .
.It Ev JAIL_CREATE_MEMORY_BYTES
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr jailctl 8
.Cm create Fl m .
.It Ev JAIL_CREATE_PROFILE
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr jailctl 8
.Cm create Fl p
.Pq one of
.Dq low ,
.Dq medium ,
or
.Dq high .
.It Ev JAIL_CREATE_RESERVED_PORTS
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr jailctl 8
.Cm create Fl r
.Pq comma-separated TCP/UDP port list .
.It Ev JAIL_SUPERVISE_FACILITY
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr jailctl 8
.Cm supervise Fl f .
.It Ev JAIL_SUPERVISE_STDOUT_LEVEL
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr jailctl 8
.Cm supervise Fl o .
.It Ev JAIL_SUPERVISE_STDERR_LEVEL
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr jailctl 8
.Cm supervise Fl e .
.It Ev JAIL_SUPERVISE_TAG
Optional value forwarded to
.Xr jailctl 8
.Cm supervise Fl t .
.It Ev JAIL_AUTOSTART
When set to
.Dq YES ,
include that jail in
.Cm start --all ,
.Cm stop --all ,
and
.Cm restart --all .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/share/examples/jailmgr/jailmgr.conf.sample"
.It Pa /etc/jailmgr.conf
Default configuration file.
.It Pa /etc/rc.d/jailmgr
Service script for boot-time start/stop of autostart-enabled jails.
.It Pa /usr/share/examples/jailmgr/jailmgr.conf.sample
Sample configuration file.
.It Pa /usr/share/examples/jailmgr/README
Operational notes and quick-start guidance.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Bring a host to operational readiness and deploy one web jail:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# jailmgr bootstrap
# jailmgr create -a -s '/usr/libexec/httpd -I 8080 -X -f -s /srv/www' -c 25 -m 512 -p medium -r 8080 -f local3 -o info -e err -t jail-web web
# jailmgr apply --ephemeral web <<'APPLY'
mkdir -p /srv/www
echo "<html>Hello NetBSD!</html>" > /srv/www/index.html
APPLY
# jailmgr config web
# jailmgr start --all
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr jailctl 8 ,
.Xr mount_null 8 ,
.Xr secmodel_jail 9 ,
.Xr rc.d 8
